---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import StickyNav from "../components/StickyNav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import CtaBanner from "../components/CtaBanner.astro";

import Reviews from "../components/Reviews.astro";
const phone = "tel:+14077343968";
const phoneDisplay = "407-734-3968";
---

<Layout
  title="Water Heater Replacement, Tankless & Gas Lines | Bonet Plumbing"
  description="Water heater replacement, tankless conversion (Rinnai, Navien, Rheem) & gas line installation in Central Florida. Same-day service. Licensed (CFC1434246). Call 407-734-3968."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", url: "https://bonetplumbing.com/" },
    { name: "Water Heaters & Gas Lines" }
  ]}
>
  <StickyNav />
  <main>
    <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-primary/[0.03] via-white to-white py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-text leading-tight mb-4">
          Water Heaters, Tankless Conversion & Gas Lines
        </h1>
        <div class="w-16 h-1 bg-accent rounded-full mb-6"></div>
        <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary mb-8 max-w-2xl">
          Out of hot water, or ready to upgrade to endless hot water with a tankless system? We replace and install water heaters across Oviedo, Winter Springs, and East Orlando — and run the gas lines that feed them, your generator, pool heater, or outdoor kitchen. Same-day service, upfront pricing, permits pulled.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 mb-10">
          <a href={phone} class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-3 bg-accent hover:bg-accent-light text-white font-bold text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-lg shadow-md transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-lg">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.25 6.75c0 8.284 6.716 15 15 15h2.25a2.25 2.25 0 002.25-2.25v-1.372c0-.516-.351-.966-.852-1.091l-4.423-1.106c-.44-.11-.902.055-1.173.417l-.97 1.293c-.282.376-.769.542-1.21.38a12.035 12.035 0 01-7.143-7.143c-.162-.441.004-.928.38-1.21l1.293-.97c.363-.271.527-.734.417-1.173L6.963 3.102a1.125 1.125 0 00-1.091-.852H4.5A2.25 2.25 0 002.25 4.5v2.25z"/>
            </svg>
            Call Now: {phoneDisplay}
          </a>
          <a href="/#contact" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-primary hover:bg-primary-light text-white font-bold text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-lg shadow-md transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-lg">
            Get a Free Estimate
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Jump links -->
        <nav aria-label="On this page" class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-12">
          <a href="#repair-replace" class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-text-secondary hover:text-primary hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">Repair & Replacement</a>
          <a href="#tankless" class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-text-secondary hover:text-primary hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">Tankless Conversion</a>
          <a href="#gas-line" class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-text-secondary hover:text-primary hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">Gas Line Installation</a>
        </nav>

        <!-- Repair & Replacement -->
        <h2 id="repair-replace" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-text mb-3">Water Heater Repair & Replacement</h2>
        <p class="text-text-secondary mb-6 max-w-2xl">
          A tank heater usually lasts 8–12 years here, and Central Florida's hard water tends to push it toward the short end of that range. If yours is leaking from the tank itself, replacement is the only real fix — and we carry quality units, install same-day, and haul the old one away.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-12">
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Water Heater Repair</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Lukewarm water, strange noises, a tripped element, or a bad thermostat? We diagnose and fix it fast — so you're not stuck taking cold showers.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Same-Day Replacement</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">If the tank is leaking or past its prime, we replace it the same day in most cases — quality units, proper code upgrades, and old-unit haul-away included.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Maintenance & Flushing</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Hard-water sediment builds up fast and kills tanks early. A regular flush extends your unit's life, quiets the rumbling, and keeps energy bills down.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Expansion Tanks & Code</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">A new heater on a closed system needs a properly sized thermal expansion tank and an up-to-code T&P discharge. We handle the details inspectors look for.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tankless -->
        <h2 id="tankless" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-text mb-3">Tankless Water Heater Conversion</h2>
        <p class="text-text-secondary mb-6 max-w-2xl">
          Tankless units heat water on demand — endless hot water, 15–20 year lifespans, lower energy bills, and a wall-mounted footprint that frees up floor space. Converting from a tank isn't just a swap, though: it usually needs an upsized gas line, proper venting, and the right sizing for your home's fixture count. We handle the whole conversion and install Rinnai, Navien, and Rheem.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-12">
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Right-Sized for Your Home</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">We size the unit to your real demand — how many showers and appliances run at once — so you get full flow without cold-water sandwiches.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Gas, Venting & Line Upsizing</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Tankless burners need more gas and dedicated venting. We upsize the gas line, run the correct venting, and bring it all to code in one job.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Rinnai · Navien · Rheem</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">We install the brands we trust and can service. We'll walk you through the differences and recommend the right fit for your home and budget.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Recirculation for Instant Hot</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Tired of waiting for hot water to reach the far bathroom? We can add a recirculation setup so it's there almost instantly — and save the water you'd run down the drain.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <CtaBanner
          heading="Ready for Endless Hot Water?"
          sub="We'll size the right tankless unit for your home and give you an honest quote — same-day service available."
        />

        <!-- Gas Line -->
        <h2 id="gas-line" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-text mb-3">Gas Line Installation & Repair</h2>
        <p class="text-text-secondary mb-6 max-w-2xl">
          Whether you're converting to tankless, adding a whole-home generator, a pool heater, an outdoor kitchen, or a gas range, it all needs a properly sized and tested gas line. We install new natural gas and propane lines, extend existing ones, and track down leaks — every job permitted, pressure-tested, and left safe.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-12">
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">New Gas Lines & Extensions</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">New runs and extensions for tankless heaters, generators, pool heaters, outdoor kitchens, ranges, and dryers — sized correctly for the appliance's demand.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Leak Detection & Repair</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Smell gas or got a high bill with no explanation? We locate the leak, repair the line, and pressure-test it before we call the job done. If you smell gas now, leave and call us.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Permitted & Pressure-Tested</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Gas work isn't the place to cut corners. We pull the permit, install to code, and pressure-test every line so it passes inspection and keeps your family safe.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-surface border border-border rounded-xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-3">Natural Gas & Propane</h3>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">We work in both natural gas and propane (LP) — including conversions and appliance hookups — across Central Florida homes.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
          <a href={phone} class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-3 bg-accent hover:bg-accent-light text-white font-bold text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-lg shadow-md transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-lg">
            Call Now: {phoneDisplay}
          </a>
          <a href="/#contact" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-primary hover:bg-primary-light text-white font-bold text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-lg shadow-md transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-lg">
            Get a Free Estimate
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ Section -->
        <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-border">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-text mb-2">How long does a water heater last?</h3>
              <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">A traditional tank water heater typically lasts 8 to 12 years, while tankless models can last 15 to 20 years with proper maintenance. Central Florida's hard water shortens tank life, so if yours is over 8 years old and needing frequent repairs, replacement is usually the better investment.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-text mb-2">Is converting to tankless worth it?</h3>
              <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">For most families, yes — you get endless hot water, lower energy bills, a longer lifespan, and reclaimed floor space. The conversion typically requires upsizing the gas line and new venting, which we handle as part of the install. We'll assess your home and give you honest numbers before you commit.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-text mb-2">Do you install gas lines for generators and outdoor kitchens?</h3>
              <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. We install and extend natural gas and propane lines for whole-home generators, pool heaters, outdoor kitchens, ranges, and dryers — each one sized for the appliance, permitted, and pressure-tested.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-text mb-2">I think I smell gas — what should I do?</h3>
              <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Leave the home, don't flip any switches, and call your gas utility and us from outside. Once it's safe, we'll locate the leak, repair the line, and pressure-test it before restoring service.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <nav class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-border" aria-label="Other services">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-text mb-4">Our Other Services</h2>
          <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <li><a href="/repiping" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light font-medium text-sm transition-colors">Whole-Home Repiping</a></li>
            <li><a href="/repiping#slab-leak" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light font-medium text-sm transition-colors">Slab Leak Repair</a></li>
            <li><a href="/repiping#sewer-line" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-light font-medium text-sm transition-colors">Sewer Line Replacement</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </section>
    <Reviews />
  </main>

  <!-- FAQPage Schema -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How long does a water heater last?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "A traditional tank water heater typically lasts 8 to 12 years, while tankless models can last 15 to 20 years with proper maintenance. Central Florida's hard water shortens tank life, so if yours is over 8 years old and needing frequent repairs, replacement is usually the better investment."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is converting to tankless worth it?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "For most families, yes — you get endless hot water, lower energy bills, a longer lifespan, and reclaimed floor space. The conversion typically requires upsizing the gas line and new venting, which we handle as part of the install. We'll assess your home and give you honest numbers before you commit."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do you install gas lines for generators and outdoor kitchens?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. We install and extend natural gas and propane lines for whole-home generators, pool heaters, outdoor kitchens, ranges, and dryers — each one sized for the appliance, permitted, and pressure-tested."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "I think I smell gas — what should I do?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Leave the home, don't flip any switches, and call your gas utility and us from outside. Once it's safe, we'll locate the leak, repair the line, and pressure-test it before restoring service."
        }
      }
    ]
  })} />

  <Footer />
</Layout>
